From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-m5 <omarchy-m5@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:50:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] irqchip/apple-aic: treat T6050 like T8142 (read-only
 VM_TMR_FIQ_ENA_EL2)

Replaces omarchy-m5 patches/linux/0002. On T6050 SYS_IMP_APL_VM_TMR_FIQ_ENA_EL2
reads back with both guest timer FIQs enabled and every write to it is
UNDEFINED. integration/aurora already handles exactly that for
apple,t8142-aic3 (vm_timer_fiq_readonly: guest timers masked through
CNT{P,V}_CTL_EL02.IMASK instead), so match apple,t6050-aic3 to the same
aic_info instead of carrying our own flag that dropped the guest timers.
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c
index 112500813..82cad3116 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-apple-aic.c
@@ -352,6 +352,14 @@ static const struct of_device_id aic_info_match[] = {
 		.compatible = "apple,t8142-aic3",
 		.data = &aic3_t8142_info,
 	},
+	{
+		/*
+		 * T6050 (M5 Pro/Max) has the same read-only, both-enabled
+		 * VM_TMR_FIQ_ENA_EL2 as T8142: every write to it is UNDEFINED.
+		 */
+		.compatible = "apple,t6050-aic3",
+		.data = &aic3_t8142_info,
+	},
 	{
 		.compatible = "apple,t8103-aic",
 		.data = &aic1_local_fipi_info,
